fn sec_cost io -> io
x10093 call open p0 13
x10094 write x10093 4
x10095 write x10094 1
x10096 text "cost"
x10097 puts x10095 x10096
x10098 call open x10097 11
x10099 write x10098 2
x10100 text "Cost"
x10101 puts x10099 x10100
x10102 call close x10101 
x10103 call open x10102 2
x10104 write x10103 4
x10105 write x10104 2
x10106 text "take"
x10107 puts x10105 x10106
x10108 write x10107 2
x10109 text "At 4000 functions an A0 edit costs 706 tokens against 143854 for TypeScript, which is 203.8x fewer than TypeScript. At 1 function A0 costs 2.42x TypeScript's tokens and 2.29x Rust's. Sonnet, cache-adjusted."
x10110 puts x10108 x10109
x10111 call close x10110 
x10112 call open x10111 2
x10113 write x10112 2
x10114 text "Cost here is every token a model reads and writes to make one edit: the instructions it is first given (the primer), the code it reads, and its reply. A model edits one function through a scoped view: the function, the signatures it depends on, and its callers. The view stays the same size as the program grows; a numbered whole file does not, so A0's advantage grows with program size and reverses on a one-function file, where the primer dominates."
x10115 puts x10113 x10114
x10116 call close x10115 
ret x10116
end

